# The owner must approve a change to these paths. Refer to "Review policy" in AGENTS.md.
# Agents open PRs with the owner's account, so GitHub does not enforce this file.
# Agents read it to know which PRs they must not merge.
# The last pattern that matches a file wins. A pattern without an owner removes the owner.

# By default, the owner approves every change: the homelab, modules, CI and the standards.
* @gsuquet

# A reviewing agent can approve documentation.
/docs/

# The standards are in the documentation, but the owner approves them.
/docs/reference/policies.md @gsuquet
/docs/reference/schemas.md @gsuquet
/docs/reference/writing-rules.md @gsuquet

# Only the owner accepts an RFC or an ADR. Refer to RFC 0001.
/docs/records/ @gsuquet

# Test and demo instances. A reviewing agent can approve them.
/instances/kind-local/
/gitops/clusters/kind-local/
